  {
    "id": "2095089513550811535",
    "text": "U.S. FUEL PRICES have risen sharply since the start of the year as simultaneous wars with Iran and between Russia and Ukraine have disrupted the global refining system. Retail gasoline prices (including taxes) are up by more than 40% compared with January while diesel prices have risen by more than 50%. In real terms, gasoline and diesel prices are now well above the long-term average having started the year significantly below it. Higher fuel prices are highly visible and impact much more heavily on households in the lower deciles of the income distribution which makes them politically sensitive:",
